# commits.env: the Corten commits kit 1999 builds (corten-run/corten), each from src-<side>/ (a
# git archive of crates examples Cargo.toml Cargo.lock .cargo at that commit) and src-<side>.commit.
#   BASE  the second placement run's base, main 14126d2a8 (#1980): the A/As, B and C's base side
#   HEAD  that run's change, one commit on BASE (#1983's buffer for an older Age): C's head side
#   X1    main 92bc32678 (#1975), the first parent of BASE's first parent a01dd5109 (a01dd5109
#         differs from it only in CONTRIBUTING.md and docs/design.md): an unpadded build only;
#         differs from BASE in crates/corten by #1980 alone (a kept answer's head held in fewer allocations; callgrind put a
#         kept hit at 32 instructions in 17,875 fewer, -0.18%, on that branch)
#   X2    705d14045, on main through #2002 (its first commit), whose parent is main 6f1bbf055: an
#         unpadded build only. In the code the probe builds it differs from BASE only in api.rs (a
#         media type read byte by byte) and compress.rs (a Cache-Control line compared with the
#         default before it is searched for no-transform); it also differs in
#         crates/corten-cli/template/Dockerfile and examples/, which the probe does not build; crates/corten/js, Cargo.lock and .cargo are BASE's,
#         so it embeds the same runtime and answers byte for byte as BASE does. Main's commits
#         just before BASE (X1's parent a02c81e86 and older) embed another runtime script, whose
#         hash is in every answer's Content-Security-Policy, so verify.sh rejects them.
BASE=14126d2a8a12bccd173ec29032c1818d42904213
HEAD=8d02090bfa2bae538394e3a36a6b941de844390c
X1=92bc326785cfb274e91302a18021902316da8cac
X2=705d140454fa800a867fda071ebc1aaead904092